<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Doubles results on the eighth day</p>
<p>of the French Open tennis tournament on Monday.</p>
<p>Prefix number denotes seeding.</p>
<p>Mixed Doubles</p>
<p>Third round:</p>
<p>4-Helena Sukova/Cyril Suk (Czech Republic) beat 12-Rita Grande</p>
<p>(Italy)/Libor Pimek (Belgium) 4-6 6-1 6-1</p>
<p>3-Manon Bollegraf (Netherlands)/Rick Leach (U.S.) beat</p>
<p>15-Mercedes Paz/Pablo Albano (Argentina) 6-2 3-6 6-3</p>
<p>Rachel McQuillan/David MacPherson (Australia) beat Patricia</p>
<p>Tarabini/Javier Frana (Argentina) 6-2 7-5</p>
<p>1-Lisa Raymond/Patrick Galbraith (U.S.) beat Kathy</p>
<p>Rinaldi-stunkel/Trevor Kronemann (U.S.) 6-3 6-3</p>
<p>9-Anna Kournikova (Russia)/Mark Knowles (Bahamas) beat Barbara</p>
<p>Rittner/Karsten Braasch (Germany) 6-4 1-6 7-5</p>
<p>Men's Doubles</p>
<p>Third round:</p>
<p>Lucas Arnold/Daniel Orsanic (Argentina) beat Olivier</p>
<p>Delaitre/Fabrice Santoro (France) 7-6 (7-1) 6-1</p>
<p>Karsten Braasch/Jens Knippschild (Germany) beat Luke</p>
<p>Jensen/Murphy Jensen (U.S.) 6-4 7-6 (7-2)</p>
<p>4-Yevgeny Kafelnikov (Russia)/Daniel Vacek (Czech Republic)</p>
<p>beat Wayne Black (Zimbabwe)/Jim Grabb (U.S.) 6-4 7-6 (7-4)</p>
<p>Tomas Carbonell/Francisco Roig (Spain) beat Sander Groen/Jan</p>
<p>Siemerink (Netherlands) 3-6 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>Women's Doubles</p>
<p>Third round:</p>
<p>5-Mary Joe Fernandez/Lisa Raymond (U.S.) beat Els Callens</p>
<p>(Belgium)/Ginger Helgeson- Nielsen (U.S.) 4-6 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>6-Nicole Arendt (U.S.)/Manon Bollegraf (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>16-Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania)/Iva Majoli (Croatia) 5-7 6-4 7-5</p>
<p>7-Yayuk Basuki (Indonesia)/Caroline Vis (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>Mercedes Paz (Argentina)/Rene Simpson (Canada) 6-4 3-6 6-3</p>
<p>4-Larisa Neiland (Latvia)/Helena Sukova (Czech Republic) beat</p>
<p>11-Naoko Kijimuta/Nana Miyagi (Japan) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>8-Alexandra Fusai/Nathalie Tauziat (France) beat 15-Anna</p>
<p>Kournikova/Elena Likhovtseva (Russia) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>10-Conchita Martinez (Spain)/Patricia Tarabini (Argentina) beat</p>
<p>2-Lindsay Davenport (U.S.)/Jana Novotna (Czech Republic) 5-7 6-4</p>
<p>6-4</p>
<p>3-Martina Hingis (Switzerland)/Arantxa Sanchez-Vicario (Spain)</p>
<p>beat Silvia Farina/Gloria Pizzichini (Italy) 6-4 6-1</p>
<p>(Ends doubles results)</p>
</text>
